{"Hello! I am Bobo. Let's read a story together!":"68462ea7f66f81b9.mp3","Hello! I am Nibbles. Let's read a story together!":"1ddc257e0d36aa80.mp3","Hello! I am Pip. Let's read a story together!":"269a150b6b6d4c48.mp3","Hello! I am Bruno. Let's read a story together!":"3acd4bf67d9e68da.mp3","Hello! I am Honey. Let's read a story together!":"0e9bc00bed30f0c2.mp3","Hello! I am Tumble. Let's read a story together!":"c01019040011fec1.mp3","Hello! I am Ducky. Let's read a story together!":"8083596721022a3e.mp3","Hello! I am Splash. Let's read a story together!":"9fa1d4f207be84f3.mp3","Hello! I am Momo. Let's read a story together!":"c0fd77b1992d589a.mp3","Hello! I am Mimi. Let's read a story together!":"13b5ff0237dea035.mp3","Hello! I am Pounce. Let's read a story together!":"7fb796c9f16bc074.mp3","Hello! I am Whiskers. Let's read a story together!":"14fcaa4af5e264cc.mp3","I don't know many words yet. Will you help me learn them?":"914d0c123e37f382.mp3","Once upon a time, there were three little pigs.":"e206e8ae9812cf8e.mp3","The first little pig built his house out of straw.":"30ef96348937f586.mp3","The second little pig built his house out of sticks.":"61d24354f98d3578.mp3","And the third little pig built his house out of strong red bricks.":"b375318f3de6d512.mp3","But then, along came a big bad wolf!":"dab34cd51d12b5de.mp3","The wolf knocked on the door. Little pig, little pig, let me come in!":"14bac514c3e7e81f.mp3","Not by the hair of my chinny chin chin!":"c64ef54113f1761d.mp3","Then I'll huff, and I'll puff, and I'll blow your house down! Blow with me! Blow into the phone!":"8c89b1503f3d2d16.mp3","Whooosh! You did it! The straw house blew away!":"2d9e4305a4c2f1d4.mp3","Whooosh! And the straw house blew away!":"c304f178b96694ac.mp3","The first little pig ran to the house made of sticks!":"f545541d27af0ea8.mp3","But the wolf huffed, and he puffed, and he blew that house down too!":"5d4cb8b9802d21cb.mp3","So both little pigs ran to the house made of bricks.":"a7a237c3a84e3ee1.mp3","The wolf huffed. And he puffed. And he huffed and he puffed.":"9e3eb676619e9024.mp3","But the brick house did not fall down. Bricks are too strong!":"b0b282ac320cb3e4.mp3","So the sneaky wolf climbed up onto the roof, and down the chimney!":"eb85b9564a60ee70.mp3","But the clever little pigs had something waiting for him.":"22ef697676cfa2b9.mp3","Splash! Right into the big hot pot!":"0316598bd4cbefca.mp3","The wolf jumped up, ran out of the door, and never ever came back!":"e0d44df2a38bd502.mp3","And the three little pigs lived happily ever after. The end!":"03f2bbe49e600cda.mp3","Look how many words you taught me! Thank you!":"35cd31be34b126ee.mp3","Ooh! What is that?":"113bfdf8857478bb.mp3","You said it! Thank you for teaching me!":"d216619ae31be266.mp3","It's a little pig!":"e123bfa0c7c0e5be.mp3","That was a pig. I will remember!":"6e14bdd021cca98a.mp3","Your turn! Can you say pig?":"79e510258a8e8839.mp3","In Spanish, we say el cerdito.":"cb3fd24825847640.mp3","pig":"e6ddc9754092cc78.mp3","In Spanish, el cerdito":"0db72739c20091ab.mp3","That house is made of straw.":"d1866add91984839.mp3","Straw. I will remember that!":"7d3c8d51bc0d6e56.mp3","Your turn! Can you say straw?":"995730c95ab67b55.mp3","In Spanish, we say la paja.":"20d8e88499ee9d43.mp3","straw":"a0fcd71b41901ded.mp3","In Spanish, la paja":"d4996f3935df760b.mp3","That house is made of sticks.":"7c571ecd31de9ec7.mp3","Sticks. I will remember that!":"ecb24f7e47aca9f7.mp3","Your turn! Can you say sticks?":"e2ef9456317faed2.mp3","In Spanish, we say los palos.":"046f30f08c12a256.mp3","sticks":"b3b4335ec36099de.mp3","In Spanish, los palos":"d84691e06e01781d.mp3","That house is made of strong bricks.":"46c1ab1218cc8bb3.mp3","Bricks. I will remember that!":"5c74d2a712844e47.mp3","Your turn! Can you say bricks?":"4c2c53e7831d460c.mp3","In Spanish, we say los ladrillos.":"a3d0e06c580800d5.mp3","bricks":"125d03c0abadab37.mp3","In Spanish, los ladrillos":"fe629a972034b8ef.mp3","It's a big bad wolf!":"22a2cd4d6c1615ea.mp3","That was a wolf. I will remember!":"8b5f9721ad5d5453.mp3","Your turn! Can you say wolf?":"e275887a03406e09.mp3","In Spanish, we say el lobo.":"f330e51c954f18af.mp3","wolf":"a463d79f90239b0c.mp3","In Spanish, el lobo":"764a8e807c065f4f.mp3","That is the chimney, on top of the roof.":"a747655c7b2bdf57.mp3","A chimney. I will remember that!":"0423b788e3fe7b3a.mp3","Your turn! Can you say chimney?":"6349743dd8a98c14.mp3","In Spanish, we say la chimenea.":"fdaab71278257889.mp3","chimney":"f88a25a6ddf3bef9.mp3","In Spanish, la chimenea":"63acf46210410c87.mp3","It's a big hot pot!":"2a63505fd3ecea6f.mp3","A pot. I will remember that!":"a90cfc7e662d037d.mp3","Your turn! Can you say pot?":"2b312ed3c066b870.mp3","In Spanish, we say la olla.":"c2d0e97a5effb9b1.mp3","pot":"1b2381313931a2fa.mp3","In Spanish, la olla":"268ff1e52d5a6e28.mp3","Who wants to come with you today?":"c1b7f1ec6108d074.mp3","Hooray! My name is Bobo!":"13b28307aecad2c6.mp3","Hooray! My name is Nibbles!":"d6d048ec8c6db15e.mp3","Hooray! My name is Pip!":"3eeceb5dd5a09d72.mp3","Hooray! My name is Bruno!":"e8a4fff9ff6c383a.mp3","Hooray! My name is Honey!":"5465d2683f91285c.mp3","Hooray! My name is Tumble!":"5555298b441c6afc.mp3","Hooray! My name is Ducky!":"a37233556e033f6e.mp3","Hooray! My name is Splash!":"ef0878dfecd52698.mp3","Hooray! My name is Momo!":"033a39d441355568.mp3","Hooray! My name is Mimi!":"aa99e82309380465.mp3","Hooray! My name is Pounce!":"783488207084f159.mp3","Hooray! My name is Whiskers!":"8b45eca376e1bb1a.mp3","What shall we call your bunny?":"7528b14f02b9f836.mp3","What shall we call your bear?":"cb789f8bd98c7bdd.mp3","What shall we call your duck?":"3486d83aec1210d7.mp3","What shall we call your cat?":"3c2c378bf230cfa5.mp3","Hello again! This one is my favourite. Will you help me learn?":"21e0a8428b76561f.mp3","In a sunny little garden, there lived an itsy bitsy spider.":"8e9dcf6f514c6a35.mp3","Beside the wall stood a tall metal water spout.":"84bde75b6ee75dca.mp3","The itsy bitsy spider wanted to climb all the way to the top.":"ae6600a1213e15b7.mp3","The itsy bitsy spider climbed up the water spout.":"3378ead91b290dbe.mp3","But high above, the sky began to fill with big grey clouds.":"0aa51032ff524d67.mp3","Down came the rain, and washed the spider out!":"c505df89d1f8f336.mp3","Poor itsy bitsy spider. She was all the way back down, and very very wet.":"0fa6580627c153fe.mp3","Can you help? Blow the rain clouds away! Blow into the phone!":"7bcc9aeedefa00d6.mp3","You did it! The clouds went whooshing away!":"24ae916f4e1c874d.mp3","And slowly, the clouds went whooshing away.":"daf67c86220010f2.mp3","Out came the sun, and dried up all the rain!":"cca824ee3b0ed7ba.mp3","The spider shook herself off. She was warm and dry again.":"7c0b5382f79f2fea.mp3","And the itsy bitsy spider climbed up the spout again!":"4b8cfe7ce55fbf6e.mp3","Up and up and up, all the way to the very top!":"d70ae270b7593425.mp3","And there, in the sunshine, she made a beautiful silver web.":"ffd5316cc318dc24.mp3","The itsy bitsy spider never ever gave up. The end!":"40795f1117effef8.mp3","You taught me so many words today! Thank you!":"3454b2ebe5a77a8e.mp3","That's a little spider!":"c949c3bef56783b0.mp3","A spider. I will remember that!":"390b765ba38e4429.mp3","Your turn! Can you say spider?":"06d664bf06956867.mp3","In Spanish, we say la araña.":"a6ddbb2f8cf595d3.mp3","spider":"be0b06090eb3e374.mp3","In Spanish, la araña":"030fbfbfa47e3bc2.mp3","That is the water spout, a big metal pipe.":"62c71549c48c6ef9.mp3","A spout. I will remember that!":"fa700720560612ec.mp3","Your turn! Can you say spout?":"3766395c74aa5e52.mp3","In Spanish, we say el canalón.":"604e35ab90100221.mp3","spout":"941a72392fef0e91.mp3","In Spanish, el canalón":"e8e0393cd1e50e0b.mp3","She is going up, up, up!":"f2915badc93a171f.mp3","Up. I will remember that!":"80b3fe8dc066e251.mp3","Your turn! Can you say up?":"dcb16e2463832da1.mp3","In Spanish, we say arriba.":"9d3983de25257e2a.mp3","up":"ab46fcfc63799a3d.mp3","In Spanish, arriba":"de0c79a213cef219.mp3","That's a big grey rain cloud.":"fce0bbe055023b5e.mp3","A cloud. I will remember that!":"c8b37eb5887dfd80.mp3","Your turn! Can you say cloud?":"a2a2a4c0d3075c36.mp3","In Spanish, we say la nube.":"e1799ab412808b51.mp3","cloud":"3a1d21272b93d626.mp3","In Spanish, la nube":"f64e9d24fc79da21.mp3","That's the rain, falling down.":"c3d31a572093f86c.mp3","Rain. I will remember that!":"7e90ef35ed27ad68.mp3","Your turn! Can you say rain?":"d0471cee8da6d05c.mp3","In Spanish, we say la lluvia.":"04a96d6b4d59f4d7.mp3","rain":"2391833b6fd01e97.mp3","In Spanish, la lluvia":"808852f03398fd21.mp3","Oh no, she washed all the way down!":"3571ab9a3dba9c43.mp3","Down. I will remember that!":"c910f48bafb9f9f5.mp3","Your turn! Can you say down?":"063f8f4e7fb1e5d9.mp3","In Spanish, we say abajo.":"ce3653182df97c7e.mp3","down":"a7a101e1d343ea35.mp3","In Spanish, abajo":"b42dc21a1c6e4405.mp3","Here comes the warm yellow sun!":"6c5b57762a1a146a.mp3","The sun. I will remember that!":"85df4bc613daf720.mp3","Your turn! Can you say sun?":"dfe7d9538e8e0d76.mp3","In Spanish, we say el sol.":"f71d12f7113d1457.mp3","sun":"db6e9f3deaa5149f.mp3","In Spanish, el sol":"b0835d86dca2cff2.mp3","She made a beautiful spider web.":"957a3b24dcbe9df7.mp3","A web. I will remember that!":"69a55b04203fc4d5.mp3","Your turn! Can you say web?":"ac7a22fea1ca48bc.mp3","In Spanish, we say la telaraña.":"3b30202f8543b855.mp3","web":"f032e03ce005b9ac.mp3","In Spanish, la telaraña":"fa0f195b43b39b81.mp3","Look, a rainbow in the sky!":"1f1fe1f6a0599c55.mp3","A rainbow. I will remember that!":"e5a14e06a6b5311f.mp3","Your turn! Can you say rainbow?":"e45b82d93d129304.mp3","In Spanish, we say el arcoíris.":"6eada5494e837e0a.mp3","rainbow":"7f45198537efc09b.mp3","In Spanish, el arcoíris":"0461f015e212b693.mp3","Ooh, this one is a chase! Come on, let's watch.":"bf9b8347ca80f845.mp3","One sunny morning, a kind old woman was baking in her little kitchen.":"94dcabf23d45e572.mp3","She rolled the dough flat, and cut out a little gingerbread man.":"586fe7850fc80173.mp3","Then she popped him into the warm oven to bake.":"a235d1f05df7dbe8.mp3","She waited, and she waited. And then something wonderful happened.":"3de28275c09f06cb.mp3","Out jumped the gingerbread man! He was alive!":"3d1060d72d010fcf.mp3","And away he ran, straight out of the door.":"d8f82d0b2407af38.mp3","Run, run, as fast as you can! You can't catch me, I'm the Gingerbread Man!":"dd34aa2c39f97715.mp3","He raced down the garden path, past all the flowers.":"c01d70886f48f1e5.mp3","He raced along the winding country lane.":"1108c0b97402dd03.mp3","He ran past a big spotty cow, munching in the meadow.":"fd5e555b91820f6a.mp3","Stop, little cake! said the cow. But the gingerbread man just laughed.":"4a58102e26a0306f.mp3","He ran past a tall brown horse, standing by the golden field.":"0d0536aa0c702df5.mp3","Stop, little cake! said the horse. But he was already gone.":"5245bb432d518b96.mp3","The farmers came running out of the barn to catch him.":"a51c03e363eec400.mp3","But nobody could catch him. He was much too fast!":"3cd4eeaf27576bfd.mp3","Over the green hill he went, laughing all the way.":"c33f25663d95d08d.mp3","Until at last, he came to a wide blue river.":"79290e975a94c0da.mp3","Oh no. Gingerbread men are not very good at swimming.":"cb6dd20ec8840cfb.mp3","Just then, a clever orange fox came padding out of the reeds.":"48e91002d040fa5b.mp3","Hop onto my back, said the fox, and I will carry you across.":"8cfe7db9ff2c13e1.mp3","So the gingerbread man hopped on, and the fox swam into the river.":"799c18167323e96c.mp3","Halfway across, the sly fox began to tip his nose up, up, up.":"594581a4d8e91d20.mp3","But the gingerbread man was quick! He jumped, and landed safe on the grass.":"65ff76acdc38ebce.mp3","And he ran, all the way home, to the kind old woman.":"a4a160f25c246768.mp3","She laughed and laughed, and gave him the biggest hug. The end!":"9788f55f529ef385.mp3","That was the best one yet! And look how many words we found.":"730bed83a085e160.mp3","oven":"c2e419385e0fe1c6.mp3","In Spanish, el horno":"eb1b43b4855fb206.mp3","run":"25d1e3260004d316.mp3","In Spanish, correr":"db0fe78829e1d347.mp3","cow":"e47949f3893694c9.mp3","In Spanish, la vaca":"e97757fec72eeacc.mp3","horse":"741f49d5f01b86a8.mp3","In Spanish, el caballo":"b58150c2e91e4700.mp3","fast":"331e63b9b7a8797a.mp3","In Spanish, rápido":"6b2169701e9556c8.mp3","river":"57f7d11b59e3ae05.mp3","In Spanish, el río":"77d4fcc4c333e63c.mp3","fox":"1c54ccc0ceffab54.mp3","In Spanish, el zorro":"31276d53794e6b70.mp3","home":"4618d41dc4439f35.mp3","In Spanish, la casa":"f6ecabcace3526ef.mp3","Say it with me. run!":"3bc1d4dc59ef0470.mp3","Yes! run!":"681ff05780ca815b.mp3","run!":"3e362ee1b3a076ce.mp3","Say it with me. cow!":"9b3d52859d7e05fd.mp3","Yes! cow!":"7e7b201a835cb5f8.mp3","cow!":"e59b7a79059ef072.mp3","Say it with me. fox!":"7384de789f1cdab9.mp3","Yes! fox!":"1071bdbbab4121cb.mp3","fox!":"22f5f21eb9c09ad7.mp3","Ooh, this one is a dream! Come and watch it with me.":"7d418604e5decd9b.mp3","On a warm summer afternoon, Alice sat by the river, feeling very sleepy.":"db9eb55df6125ef5.mp3","When all at once, a white rabbit in a red coat came hurrying by!":"2b8c1c8bc064281b.mp3","Oh my ears and whiskers! I'm late, I'm late, I'm terribly late!":"113536624dca2a90.mp3","Alice jumped up and ran after him, through the long summer grass.":"4ee42dbc4f2dc2cd.mp3","The rabbit popped straight down a great round hole, under the hedge.":"d440969fd19748f9.mp3","And Alice tumbled in after him. Down, and down, and down she went.":"2383fdbdb54c8eb4.mp3","She floated past teacups, and ticking clocks, and old picture books, all drifting in the air.":"99125253cd6f988e.mp3","Bump! Alice landed softly at the bottom, in a long hall full of little doors.":"4c90f44031ca968b.mp3","And there on a glass table, she found a tiny golden key.":"2c4abb587ef5acfb.mp3","It opened the very smallest door of all. And behind it was the loveliest garden.":"886493034d3e5655.mp3","But the door was far too little. Then Alice saw a bottle. Drink me, said the label.":"630279780e9d5f31.mp3","She took one sip, and whoosh! Alice shrank until she was as small as a mouse.":"9fc51cd8c73c0963.mp3","Then she nibbled a little cake, and up she grew, big and tall, all the way to the ceiling!":"237e6941961e34ec.mp3","At last Alice found her way out, into a garden of enormous talking flowers.":"7c791acadc9889e9.mp3","And high in a tree sat a cat, with the widest smile she had ever seen.":"56711f305aa2de87.mp3","We are all a little silly here. But don't you worry. You will find your way.":"de7181afab506a96.mp3","Then slowly, slowly, the cat faded away, until only his smile was left behind.":"83bd53c141258de9.mp3","Further along the path, the Mad Hatter and the March Hare were having a tea party.":"92aa106a4fc7951f.mp3","A very merry unbirthday to you! Have a cup, have a cake, have everything!":"3ee2687b5fa1f7a2.mp3","Then the trumpets sounded. It was the Queen of Hearts, marching through her roses.":"353b183873b64794.mp3","Everybody up! Off you go, off you go, at once!":"e60cd5558dd039d3.mp3","But her soldiers were only playing cards! Up they flew into the sky, like confetti.":"a46746facad11df8.mp3","And Alice opened her eyes. She was back by the river, warm and safe in the sunshine.":"55b86670cdb418c6.mp3","What a very curious dream, she said with a smile. The end!":"68abf71a2be71aa4.mp3","That was the best dream ever. Look at all the words we found!":"b344758cd8f15d73.mp3","Say it with me. rabbit!":"3d26c38831477e51.mp3","Yes! rabbit!":"b417c568555b934e.mp3","rabbit!":"801094f2a7655849.mp3","rabbit":"15800513fdedc76b.mp3","In Spanish, el conejo":"25d2823783d9e39a.mp3","hole":"2a9d8182654e0b74.mp3","In Spanish, el agujero":"eb9866061e44dded.mp3","key":"fc146676b45e69ee.mp3","In Spanish, la llave":"c821bf9af6613ce2.mp3","small":"92bbf1ca74fe89a0.mp3","In Spanish, pequeño":"d3d05b424538541c.mp3","big":"0f843a4736f87f0b.mp3","In Spanish, grande":"9f2def6a0273bd24.mp3","Say it with me. cat!":"b8090a28c2f440e1.mp3","Yes! cat!":"075edb20444cb050.mp3","cat!":"402e10ca9b2c25f1.mp3","cat":"7e44111a09ca3eee.mp3","In Spanish, el gato":"f01431e9e66629f6.mp3","tea":"36d8b725d66693ad.mp3","In Spanish, el té":"6b1341495b8bec5a.mp3","Say it with me. queen!":"3c65f3ce680843a1.mp3","Yes! queen!":"1264848f370af7b7.mp3","queen!":"e5eb2209af0125c1.mp3","queen":"5a9b44382de951b0.mp3","In Spanish, la reina":"64a6eae88d705883.mp3","[warmly] This one is my favourite. It is a little bit sad at the start... [brightly] but wait until the end!":"d8fad2d65785807f.mp3","[gently] Down among the tall green reeds, a mother duck sat waiting on her nest.":"632a9e0c751eca6f.mp3","[excited] Crack! Crack! Out came three tiny yellow ducklings, all fluffy and new.":"89058d68421c285d.mp3","[curiously] But the very last egg was much bigger. And out came a duckling with soft grey feathers.":"53911ebcaca50e42.mp3","[kindly] Oh! You are not yellow like the others. But you are mine, and I love you.":"fc4960e0515940f8.mp3","[warmly] The next morning, mother duck led them all down to the pond for their very first swim.":"5803e755e45ad28a.mp3","[cheerfully] Splash! The little grey one could swim beautifully. Better than all of them!":"f06ee48861e9fc09.mp3","[sadly] But the hens and the geese in the farmyard turned their backs on him.":"42ba8dcc2bffa2ac.mp3","[sadly] Why does nobody want to play with me? [quietly] Nobody at all.":"66d25a7d7663a82d.mp3","[softly] And so, as the sun went down, the little duckling felt very lonely indeed.":"0b5290e642a88c15.mp3","[gently] He walked away, far across the marshes, as the leaves turned gold and red.":"49e7deda5064c6db.mp3","[wistfully] High above him, the wild geese called to one another and flew away south.":"484d3d53882e52a9.mp3","[softly] When the rain came, he hid underneath a great green leaf, and waited.":"b2ec33aad24d2fde.mp3","[quietly] At night he saw a warm little window glowing in the dark, and he wished he had a home.":"4202a24f591d1ab8.mp3","[gently] Then the days grew colder and colder, and winter came to the marshes.":"cf0f558b7d9930fe.mp3","[carefully] The pond turned to hard shining ice, and the world went very quiet.":"c53776fadcf343b8.mp3","[warmly] A kind farmer found him shivering, and carried him into a barn full of warm straw.":"49d1437b27d3a0f8.mp3","[softly] And under all the winter stars, the little duckling slept, and waited, and grew.":"e5c426c1e39a14dc.mp3","[brightly] Then one morning the snow began to melt. The blossom opened. Spring had come at last!":"3e536b90269f5539.mp3","[wonder] And there on the water were three of the most beautiful birds he had ever seen.":"7e2b8879772d8009.mp3","[nervously] Oh, they are so lovely. They will never want me.":"e669d5568daae863.mp3","[gently] But as he came closer, he looked down into the still clear water.":"5c406f9c012614ea.mp3","[amazed] And there in the water was no grey duckling at all. There was a swan!":"fe16e2ac0df94c38.mp3","[warmly] He had been a swan all along. He was simply not grown up yet.":"8dbfd762d0d068b3.mp3","[joyfully] The three great swans curved their necks and welcomed him. You are one of us!":"b4344f3d27db2f04.mp3","[joyfully] And the children on the bank clapped their hands and said, look, that one is the most beautiful of all!":"99ee23e08821b827.mp3","[warmly] He was beautiful the whole time. He just had to grow. [brightly] Look at all our new words!":"de03eae900c23b7b.mp3","Say it with me. feather!":"ada1ea434ca2d57a.mp3","Yes! feather!":"eb05fbf966dd26f7.mp3","feather!":"1278dd2622249259.mp3","Say it with me. winter!":"0da5518c27ff5c77.mp3","Yes! winter!":"221bda2e797e01ea.mp3","winter!":"1cea0ce420d592b5.mp3","Say it with me. swan!":"b1226baa0f8c834a.mp3","Yes! swan!":"3449f44f08173811.mp3","swan!":"041cf0bf048fe429.mp3","feather":"97d843ec41c1fc28.mp3","In Spanish, la pluma":"33177cb40e020c2f.mp3","pond":"4a9bec98bbecdb2e.mp3