nd he hummed, and he smiled a very big smile indeed.":"ac620f9f693cebdd.mp3","[curiously] And slowly, one by one, the doors began to creak open.":"97c7a61a7ef10677.mp3","[curiously] What are you making? Can I see? Can I?":"348313609d80a7dc.mp3","[thoughtfully] Mmm. Wonderful. Although... I do think it would be even better with one carrot.":"439652aea3da6f5d.mp3","[brightly] Carrots! Oh, I have carrots. Wait right there!":"0b8bb7bf89eb78c7.mp3","[cheerfully] And then came potatoes. And onions. And cabbages, and beans, and barley.":"53c721decc5926e2.mp3","[warmly] The big pot bubbled and steamed until it was full right up to the brim.":"8fb2b594dc6f91c4.mp3","[delighted] And when at last they tasted it — oh! It was absolutely delicious.":"487d7125d63e283b.mp3","[joyfully] So out came the tables, up went the lanterns, and the whole village ate together.":"91f2f3dc96701a34.mp3","[warmly] Not one of them had had enough on their own. But together, there was plenty for everybody.":"eef1da768be28eaf.mp3","[gently] In the morning, the traveller waved goodbye. He had brought no food with him at all. He had brought something better. He had taught them how to share.":"3ebf9f16facc5096.mp3","[joyfully] And the little girl in the red coat kept that stone forever. The end!":"36533d12e7e30791.mp3","[warmly] A stone cannot really make soup. But it can make friends. [brightly] Look at all our new words!":"1d7e28aea2c9b742.mp3","Say it with me. village!":"05b72e7151c19ff6.mp3","Yes! village!":"fdc338a326af2c3d.mp3","village!":"ef99d43610ac9d86.mp3","Say it with me. stone!":"9c991e844456a98b.mp3","Yes! stone!":"22800b057c0d9b2c.mp3","stone!":"3e7a6b595005cec4.mp3","Say it with me. share!":"004505dc058a3fba.mp3","Yes! share!":"c83b8733e302d304.mp3","share!":"4fed09a0b0fa2512.mp3","village":"6031e7fed577d1cf.mp3","In Spanish, el pueblo":"557691ae9ec2e753.mp3","hungry":"4059eb0f00e389c4.mp3","In Spanish, hambriento":"e19b3151560b4b7b.mp3","stone":"4dcc39add2851ddf.mp3","In Spanish, la pie